FORGE

Architectural patterns in FORGE were designed by studying three MIT-licensed
open-source projects. Their ideas (not their code) shaped this implementation:

- Hermes Agent (Nous Research) - declarative provider profiles, phase-verdict
  loop structure, backend-agnostic execution environments, incident-driven
  eval culture.
- OpenCode - event-sourced state, client/server separation, inbox delivery
  semantics, structured compaction checkpoints, typed error taxonomy,
  decline-as-control-plane-signal.
- QUACK Contributors - capability-scoped grants with attenuation,
  model-proposes/runtime-executes governance, evidence->verification->receipt
  discipline, quarantine-first extension ingestion, secrets allowlisting.

All three are MIT-licensed. This project re-derived their concepts into an
original architecture (see architecture/ directory); no substantial code was
copied.
